1
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,979
Were you about to tell me something just now?

2
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,919
I'm leaving.

3
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:41,419
Have you figured out what you'll do?

4
00:02:43,419 --> 00:02:43,840
Not yet.

5
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:46,340
But I want to get out and explore.

6
00:02:48,719 --> 00:02:49,219
Sure.

7
00:02:50,259 --> 00:02:51,060
I support you.

8
00:02:59,280 --> 00:02:59,840
Um...

9
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,500
After I leave,

10
00:03:02,479 --> 00:03:03,659
I'm leaving Bite to you.

11
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,900
Don't worry, um...

12
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,539
I'll work hard to earn his living expenses,

13
00:03:08,539 --> 00:03:09,759
and I'll send the money to you every month.

14
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:13,120
I'm about to strike it rich

15
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,120
thanks to Herb Hive.

16
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,699
Money's the least of our worries.

17
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,780
If things don't work out for you out there,

18
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,759
just come back anytime.

19
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,419
Our Herb Hive team

20
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,460
will always have a spot for you.

21
00:03:22,979 --> 00:03:25,020
As if a super dad like me could fail out there.

22
00:04:04,199 --> 00:04:05,840
Here's a little something for you.

23
00:04:07,099 --> 00:04:07,400
Here.

24
00:04:09,159 --> 00:04:09,699
What is it?

25
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:11,419
Open it and take a look.

26
00:04:14,539 --> 00:04:15,719
Ugly Doll Family.

27
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:20,300
You designed them all for me.

28
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,240
This is my first original creation.

29
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,579
Don't turn your nose up at it, okay?

30
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:43,100
Thank you.

31
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:44,319
Qi Xiaowei.

32
00:04:49,459 --> 00:04:49,980
Thank you.

33
00:04:50,839 --> 00:04:51,579
Yang Xiaofang.

34
00:05:09,019 --> 00:05:10,120
Pretty impressive, Qingcang. Really.

35
00:05:11,699 --> 00:05:12,079
What?

36
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,920
I said I admire you.

37
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,060
If it were me, I couldn't do it.

38
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:18,040
You don't need to pity me.

39
00:05:18,639 --> 00:05:20,420
This isn't me letting go.

40
00:05:21,259 --> 00:05:24,240
This is my feelings leveling up.

41
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:26,040
Come on.

42
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,600
I just took the initiative to get lost, didn't I?

43
00:05:29,279 --> 00:05:30,120
What? What "get lost"?

44
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:30,779
What "get lost"?

45
00:05:31,279 --> 00:05:32,339
I can't stand hearing that word.

46
00:05:33,019 --> 00:05:34,579
Yang Youzhi told me to get lost.

47
00:05:34,939 --> 00:05:36,240
Now you're telling me to get lost too?

48
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:37,759
Who am I?

49
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:41,259
I'm Shu Qingcang.

50
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,579
I'm gonna hold up the sky.

51
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,899
Didn't you say you let go?

52
00:05:58,620 --> 00:05:59,300
You clearly haven't let go.

53
00:06:00,699 --> 00:06:02,519
I guess I still can't let go of you.

54
00:06:04,199 --> 00:06:05,319
What a lousy name I've got.

55
00:06:05,319 --> 00:06:06,199
Shu Qingcang, really?

56
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,139
I can't even hold my ground.

57
00:06:07,759 --> 00:06:08,259
I've figured it out.

58
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:10,040
My whole problem

59
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,120
lies right in this name of mine.

60
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,819
My name's just too grandiose.

61
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:16,220
Look at Xiaowei.

62
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:17,519
Xiaofang.

63
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:18,879
They've all got "little" in their names.

64
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:19,240
Take

65
00:06:20,259 --> 00:06:20,759
Xiaofang.

66
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,740
She looks all soft and delicate,

67
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:25,160
but she's incredibly tough and resilient.

68
00:06:27,439 --> 00:06:27,980
I'm changing my name.

69
00:06:28,379 --> 00:06:29,339
I'll pick a "little" name too.

70
00:06:31,779 --> 00:06:32,720
You should be called Little Grass.

71
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,339
Resilient grass, life eternal.

72
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:35,699
What a great name!

73
00:06:36,399 --> 00:06:37,180
A great name.

74
00:06:37,459 --> 00:06:38,540
It's great because... because...

75
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:41,480
It pairs perfectly with Xiaofang!

76
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,459
Get out of here!

77
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,360
I'm just kidding with you.

78
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:46,399
Fine.

79
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,279
From now on,

80
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,120
I'll aim big by starting small too.

81
00:06:50,379 --> 00:06:52,620
And keep my feet on the ground.

82
00:06:55,319 --> 00:06:56,620
Feet in the dirt feels pretty nice, actually.

83
00:07:09,319 --> 00:07:10,139
It does feel pretty grounding.

84
00:07:22,779 --> 00:07:23,660
There's something I've wondered about for ages.

85
00:07:26,819 --> 00:07:27,800
Such a beautiful, poetic scene.

86
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:29,959
Will the camera catch me in it?

87
00:07:34,819 --> 00:07:35,259
Not likely.

88
00:07:39,279 --> 00:07:39,879
Eat up.

89
00:07:42,319 --> 00:07:42,899
Have some more.

90
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:45,240
Let me feed you one last time.

91
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:47,660
Tomorrow you'll still be poultry,

92
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,100
and I'll go back to being a workhorse.

93
00:07:49,519 --> 00:07:50,779
I'm honestly worse off than you.

94
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:52,980
You're free as birds out here.

95
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:55,579
Eat.

96
00:07:57,439 --> 00:07:59,180
Dear Mom,

97
00:07:59,199 --> 00:08:00,959
I've figured it out.

98
00:08:01,259 --> 00:08:03,759
I can't stay stuck in place anymore.

99
00:08:03,959 --> 00:08:05,899
I have to be like Xiaofang,

100
00:08:05,939 --> 00:08:08,139
and find my own path in life.

101
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,060
Pessimists are often right,

102
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:11,500
but optimists make progress.

103
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,579
My ideals will be steadfast unto... what is it?

104
00:08:14,579 --> 00:08:15,079
Stop, stop reading.

105
00:08:15,079 --> 00:08:16,399
How do you say this word?

106
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,240
It's "yu." Steadfast unto death.

107
00:08:19,579 --> 00:08:20,220
Mom.

108
00:08:20,519 --> 00:08:22,300
By the classic TV-drama playbook,

109
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,279
you're supposed to wait till I've left

110
00:08:23,279 --> 00:08:24,180
before you read this letter.

111
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:25,800
At the very least, wait till tomorrow morning.

112
00:08:26,139 --> 00:08:26,680
Well then,

113
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,019
I'll read it tomorrow morning.

114
00:08:28,779 --> 00:08:29,639
Mom, Mom, Mom.

115
00:08:32,779 --> 00:08:33,440
Mom, I'm...

116
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:35,340
heading back to Shenzhen tomorrow.

117
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,440
I can tell.

118
00:08:37,899 --> 00:08:39,539
And before you go, you're sneaking off with

119
00:08:39,539 --> 00:08:41,840
my eggplants and green beans.

120
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:43,360
These are for my old coworkers.

121
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:46,840
Girl,

122
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,419
you mean that Li Xiaorou?

123
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,539
It's not just Li Xiaorou.

124
00:08:53,419 --> 00:08:54,639
There are lots of people, lots of them.

125
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:55,259
Oh, don't mess with me.

126
00:08:55,539 --> 00:08:56,279
These days,

127
00:08:56,559 --> 00:08:58,940
folks in the city keep veggies as pets.

128
00:08:59,419 --> 00:09:01,100
They say they want that rural vibe.

129
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,899
Once you're all at work,

130
00:09:03,899 --> 00:09:05,659
you don't even have time to eat.

131
00:09:06,059 --> 00:09:09,059
And you want a rural vibe?

132
00:09:09,559 --> 00:09:11,379
They'll all be dead in a few days.

133
00:09:11,679 --> 00:09:13,320
Have them add me on WeChat,

134
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:17,120
and I'll do Cloud Farming for them.

135
00:09:17,659 --> 00:09:18,399
Cloud Farming.

136
00:09:18,399 --> 00:09:20,120
You even know such a trendy term?

137
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,620
So what?

138
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,139
I've even got two crocodiles

139
00:09:23,139 --> 00:09:24,820
I'm raising over in Africa.

140
00:09:25,059 --> 00:09:25,940
Once they grow up,

141
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:27,740
they'll be mailed straight to me.

142
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,299
Mom, that one's got to be fake, right?

143
00:09:31,039 --> 00:09:31,539
Is it now?

144
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:35,779
Well, no big deal.

145
00:09:36,419 --> 00:09:38,100
As long as I don't cheat anyone.

146
00:09:42,639 --> 00:09:44,059
Once you've all left,

147
00:09:44,299 --> 00:09:46,179
I've grown so many vegetables.

148
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:49,200
Can't sell them,

149
00:09:50,019 --> 00:09:51,539
and can't eat them all either.

150
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,279
Once I've raised them well,

151
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:58,740
I'll mail them over to you all.

152
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:11,340
Mom,

153
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:13,840
I'm not leaving after all.

154
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,500
So what are you gonna do?

155
00:10:17,299 --> 00:10:18,700
Everyone loves Cloud Farming, right?

156
00:10:19,379 --> 00:10:20,340
So I'll keep my feet on the ground,

157
00:10:21,019 --> 00:10:22,039
and run one heck of a veggie garden.

158
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,120
No, I mean,

159
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,580
Grandma's Veggie Garden.

160
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,200
I'm staying.

161
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,139
Well, that's great.

162
00:10:30,919 --> 00:10:32,120
Saves me money.

163
00:10:34,139 --> 00:10:35,220
Leaving comes with cash, though.

164
00:10:36,779 --> 00:10:38,799
Then, just treat it as an investment, Mom.

165
00:10:40,899 --> 00:10:41,840
Mom, consider it buying shares.

166
00:10:42,799 --> 00:10:43,980
Mom, think about it.

167
00:10:44,659 --> 00:10:45,779
Mom, love me one more time.

168
00:10:46,379 --> 00:10:46,899
Mom.

169
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,500
Mom, love me one more time.

170
00:10:48,919 --> 00:10:49,279
Mom.

171
00:11:03,179 --> 00:11:03,960
There really are a lot.

172
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:06,019
How much is this one?

173
00:11:07,039 --> 00:11:07,899
This is the new model.

174
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:08,460
A hundred and fifty.

175
00:11:08,899 --> 00:11:09,559
That expensive?

176
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:11,960
This one's cheaper, fifty.

177
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:12,799
That one's fifty too.

178
00:11:12,799 --> 00:11:13,720
Who do you think you're looking down on?

179
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,919
I was just saying.

180
00:11:15,519 --> 00:11:16,700
Of course I'll take the hundred-and-fifty one!

181
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:17,840
My granddaughter,

182
00:11:18,299 --> 00:11:19,179
what she eats, drinks, and uses,

183
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:19,960
it all has to be the best.

184
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:20,980
Is that so?

185
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:21,860
I happen to have some change.

186
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:22,360
Let me spend it.

187
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,059
A hundred.

188
00:11:50,259 --> 00:11:50,879
Huzi!

189
00:11:51,799 --> 00:11:52,440
Huzi!

190
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,600
You've got to pull through!

191
00:11:55,419 --> 00:11:57,019
If anything happens to you,

192
00:11:58,419 --> 00:11:59,919
how am I supposed to answer for it?

193
00:12:01,779 --> 00:12:02,320
Huzi!

194
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:02,840
Uncle Qi!

195
00:12:03,379 --> 00:12:04,000
Uncle Qi!

196
00:12:04,639 --> 00:12:05,679
How's my dad?

197
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:06,440
Huzi...

198
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,399
He's still in surgery.

199
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:09,620
Wait, what happened?

200
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,500
Mom said you got in a car accident.

201
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:12,440
No.

202
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,039
Your Uncle Huzi

203
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,240
was lying on the ground,

204
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,399
sweating all over from the pain.

205
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:18,840
I didn't dare move him,

206
00:12:19,279 --> 00:12:20,519
so I called an ambulance

207
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,100
and brought him here.

208
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,559
You had a car accident.

209
00:12:23,559 --> 00:12:24,779
How come you're fine?

210
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,980
Qi Deyao, you're the one who caused it, right?

211
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:27,639
Was it you?

212
00:12:28,259 --> 00:12:28,919
Huzi!

213
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:31,779
Huzi, you've got to make it through!

214
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:34,379
Even if you're paralyzed from the neck down,

215
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:35,480
I, old Qi,

216
00:12:35,639 --> 00:12:37,379
will take care of you the rest of your life!

217
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,340
Crocodile tears! You can't get away!

218
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:41,720
Go paralyze yourself!

219
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:43,200
Huzi!

220
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,480
Doctor!

221
00:12:48,919 --> 00:12:49,639
How's my dad?

222
00:12:50,039 --> 00:12:51,200
Doctor, is he...

223
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:52,159
What's broken?

224
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:53,320
Did you reattach it?

225
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:54,659
Acute appendicitis.

226
00:12:54,759 --> 00:12:56,159
Good thing you brought him in time.

227
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,500
Any later and it would've perforated.

228
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:02,879
Appendicitis?

229
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,299
Appendicitis?

230
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:09,600
Uncle Qi...

231
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:10,399
Uncle Qi, Uncle Qi...

232
00:13:10,519 --> 00:13:10,899
He's fine now.

233
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,340
Yang Fanhu, aren't you something.

234
00:13:22,759 --> 00:13:23,600
Real good at toughing it out, huh?

235
00:13:24,419 --> 00:13:25,899
It almost perforated, you know that?

236
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,419
If Uncle Qi hadn't come today

237
00:13:28,419 --> 00:13:29,220
and brought you to the hospital,

238
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:29,740
what would you have done?

239
00:13:30,159 --> 00:13:30,960
Just kept toughing it out on the road

240
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:31,779
until you passed out?

241
00:13:31,799 --> 00:13:32,279
Right?

242
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:34,879
It's nothing.

243
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,299
They just cut out a piece

244
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:38,879
of useless intestine, right?

245
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:40,299
Don't worry.

246
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,960
That Qi Deyao,

247
00:13:45,779 --> 00:13:46,440
how's he doing?

248
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:47,980
Uncle Yang, this time

249
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:49,360
he really saved your life.

250
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,419
Your dad's so tough,

251
00:13:51,419 --> 00:13:53,440
even the King of Hell would offer him a smoke.

252
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,220
If he hadn't stuck his nose in and grabbed me,

253
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,460
I could've done a quick flip

254
00:13:56,559 --> 00:13:57,539
and dodged it clean.

255
00:13:57,580 --> 00:13:58,340
Might've even scared his car

256
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,240
to a dead stop.

257
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:00,259
Oh, really?

258
00:14:00,259 --> 00:14:01,879
Then why rush over to pay the bill now?

259
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:02,940
What are you after?

260
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:03,879
Me?

261
00:14:04,919 --> 00:14:05,919
I just want some peace and quiet.

262
00:14:07,059 --> 00:14:08,840
Call it paying for peace of mind.

263
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:10,399
I'm worried that old geezer

264
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:11,240
will use this against me

265
00:14:11,379 --> 00:14:12,580
and shake me down for big money later.

266
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:14,759
I wonder who it was

267
00:14:14,759 --> 00:14:16,200
just now outside the operating room

268
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,279
bawling their eyes out,

269
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,240
swearing to take care of Uncle Yang

270
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,080
for the rest of his life.

271
00:14:19,399 --> 00:14:20,919
Just go thank him properly.

272
00:14:20,919 --> 00:14:21,519
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

273
00:14:21,519 --> 00:14:22,639
Do you really have to be so stubborn?

274
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:26,600
If it weren't for me

275
00:14:26,639 --> 00:14:27,879
calling the ambulance in time,

276
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:29,019
that old life of his

277
00:14:29,019 --> 00:14:29,740
might not have been saved.

278
00:14:30,639 --> 00:14:31,120
Let me do it.

279
00:14:36,659 --> 00:14:37,279
You two...

280
00:14:37,759 --> 00:14:38,259
I mean,

281
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,320
First you save him,

282
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,080
then he saves you.

283
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,000
You've spent this whole life

284
00:14:42,559 --> 00:14:43,659
like a couple of squabbling rivals.

285
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,519
Bro, I really admire you.

286
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,159
Your own appendix perforated,

287
00:14:47,159 --> 00:14:47,960
and you still saved someone else.

288
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,539
You're a real hero!

289
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,019
I'm fine.

290
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,340
This old body of mine,

291
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,740
you all know it well enough, right?

292
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:57,659
Oh right, that Herb Hive of yours,

293
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,019
isn't it about to open?

294
00:14:59,299 --> 00:15:01,019
So don't hang around here.

295
00:15:01,419 --> 00:15:02,019
And you too.

296
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,620
Yakety-yak, yakety-yak.

297
00:15:03,679 --> 00:15:04,299
So annoying.

298
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:08,980
The doctor said

299
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:10,320
you need to eat something easy to digest.

300
00:15:10,679 --> 00:15:11,919
I'll go make you some noodle soup.

301
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,159
Uncle, keep an eye on him.

302
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:14,519
No need.

303
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:15,659
Besides,

304
00:15:16,639 --> 00:15:17,519
I'll have Grandma come watch over you.

305
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,159
Don't test me.

306
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:21,940
Poach a couple of eggs in it, then.

307
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,100
Huzi, Huzi.

308
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:25,200
Xiaofang, Uncle Qi.

309
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,379
Looking good.

310
00:15:30,299 --> 00:15:31,139
Yang Fanhu,

311
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:32,720
let's get one thing straight now.

312
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,879
It was your own appendix that failed you.

313
00:15:35,379 --> 00:15:36,080
It had nothing to do with me.

314
00:15:38,639 --> 00:15:39,139
Uncle Yang,

315
00:15:39,399 --> 00:15:40,399
thanks to you saving my dad,

316
00:15:40,679 --> 00:15:42,120
my dad just promised me

317
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:43,620
he'll take good care of you from now on.

318
00:15:44,379 --> 00:15:46,480
Who said that? Who? Who said it?

319
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:47,340
You did.

320
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,200
As for me and Yang Fanhu down the road,

321
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:51,279
who knows who'll be taking care of whom.

322
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,120
Are you cursing me,

323
00:15:53,139 --> 00:15:54,480
or cursing yourself?

324
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,039
What kind of talk is that?

325
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:58,039
I'll go make some noodle soup.

326
00:15:58,539 --> 00:15:59,620
Since your dad's sick of my nagging anyway,

327
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,379
I'll come along.

328
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,620
Over at Bite's place,

329
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:03,019
I need to get back and help out too.

330
00:16:03,259 --> 00:16:03,580
Hey now,

331
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,500
Why's everyone just up and leaving?

332
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,440
You get going too.

333
00:16:07,899 --> 00:16:08,419
Get lost.

334
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,399
Who'd have thought

335
00:16:12,659 --> 00:16:14,740
that I, Qi Deyao, worked myself ragged

336
00:16:14,759 --> 00:16:15,879
getting you to the hospital,

337
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,740
only to get nothing out of it,

338
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,240
and in the end wind up

339
00:16:19,659 --> 00:16:20,539
being told to get lost.

340
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:21,639
I'll get lost.

341
00:16:22,059 --> 00:16:22,779
Goodbye.

342
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,279
Goodbye.

343
00:16:46,639 --> 00:16:48,080
The, the doctor said

344
00:16:48,759 --> 00:16:49,980
you've got to move around.

345
00:16:50,659 --> 00:16:51,659
Because passing gas

346
00:16:51,659 --> 00:16:52,500
is so important for you.

347
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,299
You can't let it build up in your gut.

348
00:16:54,399 --> 00:16:55,899
You're the one full of hot air!

349
00:16:56,019 --> 00:16:57,039
The gas in my gut!

350
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:58,480
You just don't know what's good for you.

351
00:16:58,779 --> 00:17:00,200
You've got to stroll, got to walk.

352
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:01,299
Be good now, be good, be good.

353
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,460
That way you'll heal faster.

354
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,519
Pass more gas,

355
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,680
so your intestines settle back in.

356
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:05,920
Enough, quit spouting nonsense here.

357
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:06,859
Okay, okay, okay, come on now.

358
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,420
Help me up.

359
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,640
You've got a diaper on under there, right?

360
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,019
At your age, you've gotta admit you're old.

361
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:23,460
Qi Deyao,

362
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,380
Why'd you suddenly turn so nice?

363
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:29,339
Don't people always say,

364
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:30,519
A reformed prodigal is more precious than gold.

365
00:17:32,579 --> 00:17:33,660
You, a prodigal? Please.

366
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:37,920
Isn't there another saying too?

367
00:17:39,019 --> 00:17:41,359
It goes, a leopard can't change its spots.

368
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:43,859
Let me tell you,

369
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:45,680
We've been strolling for half an hour now,

370
00:17:45,799 --> 00:17:46,960
and you don't feel a thing?

371
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:48,900
Holding in all that gas,

372
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:49,640
saving it up for New Year's?

373
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:52,680
The grudge I hold against you,

374
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:54,059
I've bottled it up half my life.

375
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,079
It's not something

376
00:17:56,759 --> 00:17:58,359
I can let out in one go.

377
00:17:58,839 --> 00:17:59,660
Fine, fine.

378
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:00,920
Then don't let it out.

379
00:18:03,119 --> 00:18:04,180
Hold it till it kills you, hurts you to death.

380
00:18:06,359 --> 00:18:09,019
I haven't died from holding it or the pain yet.

381
00:18:09,279 --> 00:18:11,019
I think you'll fret yourself to death first.

382
00:18:11,779 --> 00:18:13,059
You're the one who went under the knife.

383
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:14,940
What's it got to do with me?

384
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:15,640
Why would I be fretting?

385
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:16,720
Hold on tight.

386
00:18:18,079 --> 00:18:19,039
You, you okay?

387
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:25,099
Just taking a stroll.

388
00:18:30,819 --> 00:18:31,740
Don't you dare laugh.

389
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:32,960
If you laugh,

390
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:34,259
that wound of yours will burst open.

391
00:18:34,819 --> 00:18:35,259
Get lost.

392
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:36,319
I won't.

393
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:37,400
Get lost, get lost.

394
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,039
I won't, I won't.

395
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:40,339
Get lost, get lost, get lost.

396
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:41,400
I refuse, I refuse.

397
00:18:41,799 --> 00:18:44,599
You should be called Qi the Big Scoundrel.

398
00:18:44,819 --> 00:18:46,299
And you should be called Yang the Ingrate.

399
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,519
Folks, it's not that I don't want to sell it

400
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,359
It's these herbal dolls

401
00:21:34,599 --> 00:21:35,440
We're all out of stock right now

402
00:21:36,039 --> 00:21:37,259
Given my relationship with Xiaofang

403
00:21:37,279 --> 00:21:38,039
Once new stock comes in

404
00:21:38,339 --> 00:21:39,980
She'll definitely save some for me first

405
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:40,759
All right then

406
00:21:41,339 --> 00:21:42,980
That's it for old Qi's livestream today

407
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:44,420
See you tomorrow, same time

408
00:21:45,319 --> 00:21:46,059
Love you all!

409
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,039
Haiyun

410
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,059
We clearly have stock

411
00:21:55,079 --> 00:21:56,200
So why won't you let me sell it?

412
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,160
Now that's something you don't get

413
00:21:58,339 --> 00:21:59,680
It's called Hunger Marketing.

414
00:22:00,279 --> 00:22:00,960
Just follow

415
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,200
the script I gave you and read it

416
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:02,980
You can't go wrong

417
00:22:03,859 --> 00:22:04,759
Don't just stand there

418
00:22:05,099 --> 00:22:05,859
Hurry up and go over

419
00:22:05,859 --> 00:22:07,339
the script for the next session

420
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:09,980
Come on, old-timer, do it right

421
00:22:10,299 --> 00:22:11,039
Keep up the good work

422
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:12,660
Show a little more energy

423
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:15,000
Mom

424
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:17,180
Mom

425
00:22:17,579 --> 00:22:18,619
There's another session this afternoon

426
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:20,019
Don't forget your flower arranging class

427
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:23,039
Got it

428
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:52,099
Hold on a sec, bro.

429
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:53,059
Let's adjust this a bit more.

430
00:22:53,079 --> 00:22:54,160
Good, side profile, jawline.

431
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,299
Nice, perfect.

432
00:22:55,359 --> 00:22:57,359
Okay, three, two, one.

433
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:58,359
Action.

434
00:22:58,599 --> 00:22:59,539
Time...

435
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:01,920
is the ultimate extractor.

436
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,680
Atop Fairy Peak,

437
00:23:04,380 --> 00:23:05,839
clad in mist and cloud.

438
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,240
The Authentic Series.

439
00:23:10,019 --> 00:23:13,039
We don't pander. We conquer.

440
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:15,319
Cut.

441
00:23:15,819 --> 00:23:16,720
Let's do another take, bro.

442
00:23:16,799 --> 00:23:17,720
It's just that this video

443
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:18,380
is greasy enough to fry veggies.

444
00:23:18,559 --> 00:23:19,599
How vulgar.

445
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,259
The world doesn't get my performance art.

446
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:24,380
I can't take it anymore.

447
00:23:24,819 --> 00:23:25,759
Just stop talking, okay?

448
00:23:25,759 --> 00:23:27,059
Come on, my performance art is great!

449
00:23:27,059 --> 00:23:27,859
You've turned our account

450
00:23:27,859 --> 00:23:28,960
into your own personal life

451
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:29,740
sharing show.

452
00:23:29,980 --> 00:23:31,339
Let me tell you, let me tell you.

453
00:23:31,779 --> 00:23:33,220
Don't call it greasy, don't call it that.

454
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:33,579
Let me tell you,

455
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:34,440
under my, Shu Xiaocao's,

456
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,500
official leadership,

457
00:23:35,839 --> 00:23:37,400
this month, compared to last month,

458
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:40,619
our sales are up 50 percent.

459
00:23:41,259 --> 00:23:42,359
The boss has got it all handled.

460
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,140
Great.

461
00:23:43,339 --> 00:23:43,880
At the end of this month,

462
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:45,380
we shareholders get dividends.

463
00:23:45,819 --> 00:23:47,940
Thank you, Boss Fang, thank you.

464
00:23:50,839 --> 00:23:51,440
Granny.

465
00:23:52,359 --> 00:23:53,940
These hands of yours now

466
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:55,339
are Fairy Peak's

467
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:57,339
most vital productivity tool.

468
00:23:57,819 --> 00:23:59,440
The Green Bean Terminator.

469
00:24:00,779 --> 00:24:01,339
Jingjing.

470
00:24:01,819 --> 00:24:03,000
This thing is great.

471
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,420
I've lived my whole life,

472
00:24:04,839 --> 00:24:07,059
never knew nails could be weapons.

473
00:24:07,900 --> 00:24:08,660
Xiaofang's here.

474
00:24:10,380 --> 00:24:11,500
Xiaofang.

475
00:24:11,579 --> 00:24:13,319
There's a line at the door, Jingjing.

476
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,619
Grandma, Auntie.

477
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:15,940
Thank you.

478
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,059
I'll just put these here then.

479
00:24:19,019 --> 00:24:20,660
Upgraded the gear again.

480
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,559
This is tech empowering traditional farming.

481
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:24,460
Jingjing says

482
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:26,119
using this to pinch green beans

483
00:24:26,519 --> 00:24:28,039
makes it twice as fast.

484
00:24:28,559 --> 00:24:30,960
And saves time for a few rounds of mahjong.

485
00:24:31,180 --> 00:24:33,259
That's a self-drawn winning hand.

486
00:24:33,259 --> 00:24:33,539
A win!

487
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:35,460
Set up a table back home.

488
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:39,059
So many people here.

489
00:24:39,859 --> 00:24:41,140
Holding hands, look.

490
00:24:41,779 --> 00:24:42,559
So sweet.

491
00:24:42,599 --> 00:24:43,299
They got their marriage license.

492
00:24:43,980 --> 00:24:45,660
Brought the bride for bridal nails.

493
00:24:45,779 --> 00:24:46,400
Let's celebrate.

494
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,220
Congrats, congrats!

495
00:24:47,299 --> 00:24:48,039
Congratulations.

496
00:24:48,039 --> 00:24:49,180
The bride comes first.

497
00:24:49,319 --> 00:24:50,619
Hurry, do her nails.

498
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:52,180
Yes, yes, gotta get her set up.

499
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:53,220
The prettiest nails.

500
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:02,220
Uncle.

501
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:04,059
Whose veggie garden are you working on?

502
00:25:04,099 --> 00:25:05,019
You're so invested.

503
00:25:06,359 --> 00:25:07,519
It's Xiaorou's garden.

504
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,099
Did Xiaorou like your Moments post

505
00:25:09,099 --> 00:25:09,859
on social media?

506
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,420
Our relationship

507
00:25:11,420 --> 00:25:12,440
doesn't need likes anymore

508
00:25:12,440 --> 00:25:13,200
to prove itself.

509
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:19,960
Hello.

510
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:21,500
Hello, Xiaorou.

511
00:25:22,259 --> 00:25:23,160
The veggies are ready to harvest.

512
00:25:24,660 --> 00:25:26,279
Sure, come harvest them with me.

513
00:25:41,599 --> 00:25:42,259
So, how about it?

514
00:25:42,259 --> 00:25:43,220
Look at me, playing matchmaker.

515
00:25:43,740 --> 00:25:45,079
Don't I deserve a little reward?

516
00:25:52,019 --> 00:25:53,319
You came to see me.

517
00:25:54,380 --> 00:25:56,039
I sure didn't come to see you.

518
00:25:56,079 --> 00:25:57,700
I came to see the vegetable garden.

519
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,259
And to check on you while I'm at it.

520
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,180
Come on, let's go, go, go.

521
00:26:03,420 --> 00:26:03,759
Let's go.

522
00:26:05,799 --> 00:26:06,339
The bag, the bag.

523
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:07,240
Give me the bag.

524
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:08,059
Off we go.

525
00:26:17,259 --> 00:26:18,960
All right, easy does it.

526
00:26:19,339 --> 00:26:20,099
Come on, Grandma.

527
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:21,740
After you, Xiaorou.

528
00:26:21,960 --> 00:26:22,319
Let's go.

529
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,420
We're here, we're here.

530
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:27,119
Look, look at that.

531
00:26:27,619 --> 00:26:28,559
What's going on over there?

532
00:26:29,380 --> 00:26:30,160
Slow down, don't fall.

533
00:26:30,599 --> 00:26:31,460
Don't worry about it, I'll go.

534
00:26:31,460 --> 00:26:32,880
Old Qian, you're kicking away the ladder!

535
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:34,079
You've got no loyalty!

536
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:35,859
You've got no loyalty at all!

537
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:36,200
What'd you do this time?

538
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,000
Making his mom mad again.

539
00:26:37,579 --> 00:26:38,880
Come here, you.

540
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:41,700
If you don't do your homework properly,

541
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:45,859
Grandma will use her Bean-Pinching Kung Fu on you.

542
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:46,579
Watch out.

543
00:26:46,839 --> 00:26:48,359
Nobody's here to protect you now, huh?

544
00:26:48,779 --> 00:26:49,880
You little troublemaker.

545
00:26:50,599 --> 00:26:51,119
Keep running, why don't you.

546
00:26:51,420 --> 00:26:51,940
Stop right there!

547
00:26:52,079 --> 00:26:52,599
Still running?

548
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:53,880
Careful, you'll fall again.

549
00:26:54,559 --> 00:26:55,559
Help! Somebody help!

550
00:27:14,579 --> 00:27:15,000
All right.

551
00:27:15,339 --> 00:27:16,480
He's asleep.

552
00:27:17,480 --> 00:27:18,859
Now it's time for me,

553
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,720
Yang Xiaofang, the goddess of mahjong.

554
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:22,380
Get ready to bleed cash, everyone.

555
00:27:22,519 --> 00:27:23,720
Come on, come on, sit down.

556
00:27:23,720 --> 00:27:24,960
We've been waiting ages for you.

557
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:32,099
Here.

558
00:27:36,099 --> 00:27:36,839
Come on, have a taste.

559
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:39,200
Here.

560
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:41,380
Is it good?

561
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:42,579
Sour.

562
00:27:43,059 --> 00:27:43,559
So sour.

563
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:45,359
Old Qian came back this time

564
00:27:45,460 --> 00:27:46,339
looking pretty lively.

565
00:27:46,619 --> 00:27:48,619
No more hiding all over the place.

566
00:27:49,380 --> 00:27:49,920
That's right.

567
00:27:50,180 --> 00:27:51,319
Thanks to my clothing shop,

568
00:27:51,759 --> 00:27:53,279
I guess he's back on his feet again.

569
00:27:53,819 --> 00:27:54,859
Let's see if he ever dares to dump

570
00:27:54,859 --> 00:27:55,759
me and Dandan again.

571
00:27:56,259 --> 00:27:58,200
Nothing beats earning your own money.

572
00:27:58,640 --> 00:27:59,099
Five Characters.

573
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,359
It's sweeter than what a man gives you.

574
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,319
One Character.

575
00:28:05,359 --> 00:28:06,019
Where's your mom?

576
00:28:06,460 --> 00:28:07,359
Why hasn't she come back?

577
00:28:07,900 --> 00:28:09,200
You've really hit the nail on the head.

578
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:09,920
Just look.

579
00:28:10,799 --> 00:28:11,839
Every single day with those elephants,

580
00:28:11,839 --> 00:28:12,720
hanging out together,

581
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:14,200
She won't even reply to my WeChat.

582
00:28:14,259 --> 00:28:14,920
Look, look.

583
00:28:15,099 --> 00:28:15,920
So carefree.

584
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:19,200
Let me tell you all,

585
00:28:19,279 --> 00:28:21,279
Fanzhu and Xiaorou

586
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:23,319
have already met each other's parents.

587
00:28:23,599 --> 00:28:24,220
So next,

588
00:28:24,420 --> 00:28:26,059
the bride price and the wedding,

589
00:28:26,059 --> 00:28:27,200
can't be taken lightly.

590
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:28,599
You all need to give some ideas.

591
00:28:28,859 --> 00:28:30,259
Let's discuss this properly.

592
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:33,400
Young people's own affairs

593
00:28:33,539 --> 00:28:34,539
should be left to those involved

594
00:28:34,579 --> 00:28:35,680
to decide for themselves.

595
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:37,640
Don't let it be like Xiaofang last time.

596
00:28:39,619 --> 00:28:40,339
Like what?

597
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:42,799
Xiaowei and I broke up,

598
00:28:42,799 --> 00:28:43,980
That wasn't because of the bride price, was it?

599
00:28:45,099 --> 00:28:46,339
But like Grandma just said,

600
00:28:46,339 --> 00:28:47,380
the goodwill we should offer

601
00:28:47,380 --> 00:28:48,299
and the respect can't be skipped,

602
00:28:48,799 --> 00:28:50,000
but we shouldn't meddle in everything.

603
00:28:51,519 --> 00:28:52,279
Come on, whose turn is it?

604
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:52,980
Who threw out the Five Dots?

605
00:28:54,059 --> 00:28:55,680
It was me, my old eyes are blurry.

606
00:28:55,680 --> 00:28:56,339
No take-backs.

607
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,259
You can't take it back, no way.

608
00:28:57,339 --> 00:28:58,940
Grandma, no cheating allowed.

609
00:28:58,980 --> 00:29:00,619
You can't cheat, you know.

610
00:29:01,339 --> 00:29:02,019
My little uncle and aunt

611
00:29:02,019 --> 00:29:03,079
are kissing outside!

612
00:29:04,339 --> 00:29:04,680
What?

613
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:05,859
My little uncle and aunt

614
00:29:05,859 --> 00:29:06,740
are kissing outside!

615
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,039
Kissing?

616
00:29:08,339 --> 00:29:09,220
That fast?

617
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:12,299
Would, would it be okay for me to go look?

618
00:29:25,480 --> 00:29:26,059
Let me do it.

619
00:29:48,579 --> 00:29:49,660
Shoo, shoo, shoo! Get inside!

620
00:29:50,559 --> 00:29:50,940
Get back inside.

621
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:52,200
Uncle, um...

622
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:53,440
Want some melon?

623
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:53,960
Um...

624
00:29:54,759 --> 00:29:55,579
Didn't I already give you melon?

625
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:57,220
Why is your face so red?

626
00:29:57,220 --> 00:29:57,539
He's been drinking.

627
00:29:57,779 --> 00:29:58,500
Exactly.

628
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:00,079
Like he's wearing blush.

629
00:30:00,279 --> 00:30:00,940
Just one little kiss...

630
00:30:00,940 --> 00:30:02,240
and he's already this tipsy?

631
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:04,279
That little rascal.

632
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,799
He sneaked and drank all the Cili Wine

633
00:30:06,839 --> 00:30:08,200
we brewed last year.

634
00:30:09,359 --> 00:30:11,099
Xiaorou, he doesn't know any better.

635
00:30:11,259 --> 00:30:12,480
He didn't make you drink too much, did he?

636
00:30:12,799 --> 00:30:13,599
Don't worry, Auntie.

637
00:30:14,039 --> 00:30:15,480
Fanzhu's no match for me.

638
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,579
Auntie, you're amazing!

639
00:30:25,619 --> 00:30:26,700
The whole family's here,

640
00:30:26,759 --> 00:30:27,759
so lively!

641
00:30:27,799 --> 00:30:28,940
Auntie, Mom, Sis!

642
00:30:29,559 --> 00:30:30,700
How come you're back?

643
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:34,059
Not looking after the elephants anymore?

644
00:30:35,099 --> 00:30:36,759
The elephants we rescued

645
00:30:36,779 --> 00:30:38,000
have all gone back to the herd,

646
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:38,940
off traveling around.

647
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,000
So I came back to check on

648
00:30:40,220 --> 00:30:42,599
the old and young elephants.

649
00:30:43,599 --> 00:30:44,740
Okay, okay.

650
00:30:44,859 --> 00:30:45,920
That's great.

651
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:47,220
Mom.

652
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:49,319
Let's get back to the table.

653
00:30:49,859 --> 00:30:50,319
Grandma.

654
00:30:50,319 --> 00:30:51,640
What did you say we needed to discuss?

655
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,599
Discuss what?

656
00:30:52,799 --> 00:30:55,299
Nothing beats a good round of mahjong.

657
00:30:55,619 --> 00:30:57,640
Let's just enjoy the moment.

658
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,359
Come on, enjoy the moment.

659
00:30:59,740 --> 00:31:00,859
The moment.

660
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:01,859
Let's not go up yet.

661
00:31:02,859 --> 00:31:03,759
We're not done talking.

662
00:31:04,819 --> 00:31:05,880
Where's our Bite?

663
00:31:06,420 --> 00:31:07,240
I'll go check on Bite.

664
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:11,039
Dandan!

665
00:31:11,740 --> 00:31:12,220
I'm not here!

666
00:31:12,220 --> 00:31:12,940
Get down here, come on!

667
00:31:13,539 --> 00:31:14,200
Hurry up!

668
00:31:14,279 --> 00:31:15,180
Come on, quick!

669
00:31:16,299 --> 00:31:17,160
Didn't we agree today

670
00:31:17,660 --> 00:31:18,500
that the guys would do the work?

671
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:19,740
Get down here!

672
00:31:19,819 --> 00:31:20,180
No way!

673
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:21,319
Except for your uncle...

674
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:22,099
Come on, come on, get down!

675
00:31:22,519 --> 00:31:22,859
So how is it?

676
00:31:23,319 --> 00:31:24,960
Working the fields, isn't it fresh?

677
00:31:25,460 --> 00:31:26,740
You call this working the fields?

678
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:27,680
This is marrying way beneath me.

679
00:31:28,380 --> 00:31:30,019
Beneath you? I'll teach you!

680
00:31:30,980 --> 00:31:31,519
Get over here!

681
00:31:32,019 --> 00:31:33,480
Too busy flirting

682
00:31:33,799 --> 00:31:35,279
and forgot to pick the green beans.

683
00:31:36,859 --> 00:31:37,279
Auntie.

684
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:39,079
No wonder you all live

685
00:31:39,079 --> 00:31:39,859
so carefree.

686
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:41,440
This scenery is just too beautiful!

687
00:31:43,519 --> 00:31:44,740
Carefree, my foot.

688
00:31:44,859 --> 00:31:46,660
That's all just for show.

689
00:31:46,980 --> 00:31:48,319
Every single one of them

690
00:31:48,519 --> 00:31:50,240
has ambitions higher than the sky.

691
00:31:52,099 --> 00:31:53,019
Fanhu

692
00:31:53,339 --> 00:31:54,839
is a stubborn mule, that one.

693
00:31:55,019 --> 00:31:57,420
Fanyan, her pride reaches the heavens.

694
00:31:57,740 --> 00:32:00,299
Half her life spent battling for face.

695
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:02,599
And Fanmei? A scheming little abacus.

696
00:32:03,019 --> 00:32:05,599
Nobody can out-calculate her.

697
00:32:06,859 --> 00:32:07,460
Fanzhu

698
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:10,279
has a whole basket of twisted logic.

699
00:32:10,759 --> 00:32:11,599
Purely

700
00:32:12,660 --> 00:32:13,579
a bully at home, coward outside.

701
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:15,880
Mom!

702
00:32:16,099 --> 00:32:16,940
Don't go airing people's flaws!

703
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:19,119
Here, sit.

704
00:32:20,259 --> 00:32:21,039
Have some fruit.

705
00:32:21,039 --> 00:32:21,519
Sure.

706
00:32:23,180 --> 00:32:24,519
Back in those days

707
00:32:25,079 --> 00:32:26,099
you just goofed around wildly.

708
00:32:26,460 --> 00:32:29,099
You ignored everything your dad said.

709
00:32:29,319 --> 00:32:31,119
In one ear and out the other.

710
00:32:32,259 --> 00:32:32,920
My dad, you know,

711
00:32:33,079 --> 00:32:34,539
never really liked talking to me.

712
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:36,400
His favorite was Xiaofang.

713
00:32:36,700 --> 00:32:38,220
Since childhood, Xiaofang went with him

714
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:38,960
up the mountain to gather herbs.

715
00:32:39,380 --> 00:32:40,039
So clever, she was.

716
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:41,359
Every single herb,

717
00:32:41,579 --> 00:32:42,339
tell her just once

718
00:32:42,619 --> 00:32:43,680
and she'd remember its name.

719
00:32:45,140 --> 00:32:46,019
My dad said

720
00:32:46,839 --> 00:32:48,539
Xiaofang was like the herbs on this mountain.

721
00:32:49,140 --> 00:32:49,680
When the wind comes,

722
00:32:50,180 --> 00:32:50,900
she can hold her ground.

723
00:32:51,700 --> 00:32:52,880
When the rain comes, it can't soak through.

724
00:32:54,160 --> 00:32:54,980
He said Xiaofang

725
00:32:55,420 --> 00:32:56,500
always carries a certain

726
00:32:56,720 --> 00:32:57,980
toughness and resilience.

727
00:33:13,099 --> 00:33:13,559
Dad,

728
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:16,099
Still cutting rice for Uncle Lin, huh?

729
00:33:16,940 --> 00:33:18,539
His legs aren't in great shape.

730
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,819
Every little bit of help counts, right?

731
00:33:21,940 --> 00:33:23,220
Guess what I brought for you.

732
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:25,619
What?

733
00:33:30,299 --> 00:33:31,240
A little something for my old man.

734
00:33:31,559 --> 00:33:32,099
That's right.

735
00:33:32,460 --> 00:33:33,099
This is the Cili Wine

736
00:33:33,099 --> 00:33:34,019
that the four of us brewed.

737
00:33:34,740 --> 00:33:36,079
You've always wanted to try it, right?

738
00:33:36,079 --> 00:33:37,559
So here, I brought it over first thing.

739
00:33:39,279 --> 00:33:40,180
That's my good girl.

740
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:44,819
Of course I had to bring it like this.

741
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:48,920
Sit down.

742
00:33:51,180 --> 00:33:52,019
Let me pour you a glass.

743
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:15,559
Right here, right now

744
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:18,420
I really feel like reciting a poem!

745
00:34:18,460 --> 00:34:19,000
Go ahead.

746
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:25,739
Fine wine's sweet aroma

747
00:34:26,860 --> 00:34:28,480
Golden rice fields aglow

748
00:34:29,179 --> 00:34:32,719
I wouldn't trade this for being village chief!

749
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:35,239
Then again

750
00:34:35,639 --> 00:34:37,679
that village chief might not even want the job.

751
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:48,980
Dad,

752
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:50,760
There's something I want to do

753
00:34:52,059 --> 00:34:53,460
But I'm not quite sure about it

754
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:55,139
Just do it

755
00:34:55,699 --> 00:34:56,599
I'm behind you all the way

756
00:34:57,719 --> 00:34:59,519
Do you even know what it is?

757
00:35:01,519 --> 00:35:02,280
Kid,

758
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:04,219
Look,

759
00:35:05,159 --> 00:35:06,800
When the rice is ripe

760
00:35:07,900 --> 00:35:10,900
you harvest it, right?

761
00:35:12,619 --> 00:35:13,659
Remember this

762
00:35:14,519 --> 00:35:15,400
For anything at all

763
00:35:16,099 --> 00:35:17,800
the moment you get the urge to do it

764
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:19,579
it means

765
00:35:20,340 --> 00:35:21,820
the time has come

766
00:35:26,340 --> 00:35:27,559
Herb Hive is going further and further

767
00:35:27,719 --> 00:35:28,980
and the business keeps growing bigger

768
00:35:29,539 --> 00:35:31,099
The herbs can barely keep up with demand

769
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:32,340
So I was thinking

770
00:35:32,980 --> 00:35:34,699
maybe we build one right here at home

771
00:35:34,699 --> 00:35:35,539
an herb-growing base

772
00:35:36,079 --> 00:35:36,840
That way, for one thing

773
00:35:37,039 --> 00:35:38,440
the quality and yield of the herbs

774
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:39,179
would both be guaranteed

775
00:35:39,519 --> 00:35:40,079
And for another

776
00:35:40,179 --> 00:35:41,260
the folks here wouldn't have to

777
00:35:41,300 --> 00:35:42,699
trek over mountains to gather herbs

778
00:35:43,239 --> 00:35:45,019
They'd have work right at their doorstep

779
00:35:45,300 --> 00:35:45,900
and money to earn

780
00:35:46,199 --> 00:35:47,500
But then I worry

781
00:35:47,860 --> 00:35:48,559
whether all at once

782
00:35:48,639 --> 00:35:49,699
we'd be biting off more than we can chew

783
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:53,079
Xiaofang

784
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:55,960
Do you remember that year

785
00:35:56,400 --> 00:35:57,079
when you were at the village entrance

786
00:35:57,139 --> 00:35:58,400
coming to bring me back home?

787
00:35:59,340 --> 00:36:00,119
Back then

788
00:36:00,639 --> 00:36:02,340
what was it you said again?

789
00:36:32,260 --> 00:36:32,860
Yang Fanhu

790
00:36:33,539 --> 00:36:33,880
Here!

791
00:36:48,340 --> 00:36:48,719
Dad.

792
00:37:03,679 --> 00:37:04,099
Let's go home.

793
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:04,579
Okay.

794
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:06,260
Okay.

795
00:37:09,500 --> 00:37:10,179
Alright, alright.

796
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:19,340
Sesame oil, two yuan.

797
00:37:19,579 --> 00:37:20,739
Two yuan, and that soap too.

798
00:37:21,219 --> 00:37:22,099
The soap's three yuan.

799
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:22,679
Got it.

800
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:27,840
Yang Fanhu.

801
00:37:28,199 --> 00:37:29,539
When did he get out of prison?

802
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:30,420
No idea.

803
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,519
I heard his wife...

804
00:37:31,519 --> 00:37:32,500
She ran off years ago.

805
00:37:33,300 --> 00:37:34,559
How's that kid supposed to get by?

806
00:37:34,599 --> 00:37:35,579
Stuck with a dad like that.

807
00:37:36,559 --> 00:37:37,980
She's the girl of a convict.

808
00:37:38,219 --> 00:37:39,219
Don't you go playing with her anymore.

809
00:37:39,679 --> 00:37:40,280
You hear me?

810
00:37:45,619 --> 00:37:47,900
Give me a pack of the cheapest ones.

811
00:37:49,159 --> 00:37:50,059
Three-fifty.

812
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:00,760
The best cigarettes for my dad.

813
00:38:01,519 --> 00:38:02,280
The best ones.

814
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,400
Here, take it.

815
00:38:23,300 --> 00:38:24,380
Grandpa told me

816
00:38:26,639 --> 00:38:28,739
that if you feel sad after you come back,

817
00:38:29,239 --> 00:38:30,199
I should tell you this.

818
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:33,019
Son,

819
00:38:34,500 --> 00:38:35,579
from now on,

820
00:38:36,219 --> 00:38:37,739
we two won't be seeing each other anymore.

821
00:38:39,019 --> 00:38:40,360
But don't be afraid.

822
00:38:41,619 --> 00:38:42,440
Just do it!

823
00:38:59,219 --> 00:38:59,559
Dad!

824
00:38:59,860 --> 00:39:00,480
Don't be afraid!

825
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,219
Just do it!

826
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:09,480
Say it out loud!

827
00:39:15,300 --> 00:39:17,900
Don't be afraid, just do it!

828
00:39:19,860 --> 00:39:21,400
Say it louder!

829
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:27,780
Don't be afraid, just do it!

830
00:39:29,659 --> 00:39:30,400
Shout it out!

831
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:32,760
Don't be afraid!

832
00:39:33,940 --> 00:39:35,539
Just do it!

833
00:39:36,079 --> 00:39:37,179
Don't be afraid!

834
00:39:38,539 --> 00:39:40,420
Just do it!

835
00:39:59,579 --> 00:40:01,300
I want to swap it for the best pinwheel.

836
00:40:14,559 --> 00:40:15,199
Xiaofang!

837
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,780
Go, go, go!

838
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,320
Let's do this together!

839
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:25,179
I know what to do now.

840
00:41:07,019 --> 00:41:14,059
Sister, go forward boldly!

841
00:41:14,699 --> 00:41:17,280
Go forward,

842
00:41:18,260 --> 00:41:23,840
And don't look back!

843
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:11,380
What is this thing, Xiaofang?

844
00:42:12,380 --> 00:42:13,039
Uncle Lei.

845
00:42:13,599 --> 00:42:14,579
Have you ever heard about

846
00:42:14,619 --> 00:42:15,559
that circus a while back,

847
00:42:15,599 --> 00:42:16,940
the one that lost a monkey?

848
00:42:17,300 --> 00:42:17,900
I know about that.

849
00:42:18,619 --> 00:42:20,260
Wasn't it carrying a speaker?

850
00:42:23,579 --> 00:42:25,000
This might be that very speaker.

851
00:42:26,260 --> 00:42:27,239
So what about the monkey?

852
00:42:30,659 --> 00:42:31,840
The monkey went home, of course.

853
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:35,139
